Attribution notes

No third-party runtime dependency is bundled. SHARDEX.md states the contract
this is measured against: "Stdlib only. No key, no build, no network." The
mirror, shatter, forge, tune and verify rungs (`shardex.py`, `ops.py`,
`meshscene.py`, `transubstantiate.py`) run on the Python standard library, and
the forged `flame.html` shell runs on the browser's own JavaScript with no
external script, font or stylesheet reference.

The rendered artefacts this project can produce (`flame/`, `.shardex/`,
`.transub/`, `.live/` and any `*.mp4` or captured frame) are generated output,
not part of the licensed source. They are gitignored and regenerated by the
commands in SHARDEX.md.

The 1966 program named in the licence discussion of sibling projects is not
referenced, included or transcribed here.

Fidelity statement, carried because a NOTICE that omits it would let the
marketing write itself: SHARDEX does not extract a game's rules. It derives a
deterministic arena from a shard's own content hash and provides a golden state
hash that independent implementations must agree on. SHARDEX.md's "honest
boundary" section is part of this distribution and governs what may be claimed.

Uninstall: delete `Project_SHARDEX/` and any `.shardex/`, `flame/`, `.transub/`
or `.live/` directory generated from it. There is no service, no registry entry
and no `site-packages` copy.
